# J34 — Run Focus / replay stage-label ordering (P3)
#
# Keyless deterministic core via F4's seeded runs. The escalated run's items.jsonl
# carries the three verify:finding stage labels in execution order; the refused
# run carries gate + panel + a refusal danger notice and NO completed escalation
# stage.
#
# Note: the offline demo target path is process-scoped (kuzushi-demo-<pid>-…), so
# a cross-process `runs trace` cannot reach these runs keyless — the in-TUI replay
# is the deterministic proof, and the shared-core content is additionally covered
# by the fixture cargo test (f4_seeds_… in devex_phase_fixture/tests.rs).
#
# Width variants (operator matrix): re-run with `--size 60x20` (stacked
# Steps/Output — labels must survive) and `--size 48x16` (single Tab-switched
# viewport — Tab to Output, stage labels still present).
#
# J34-L (advisory, live): with a real key, `setg VERIFY_PASSES 2` + a distinct
# escalationModel, run a real verify and capture Run Focus mid-flight; accept
# SKIP and accept that a real panel may not split.
name: replay renders the verify stage ladder in gate-panel-escalation order
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_DEVEX_PHASE_FIXTURE=1
launch:
wait-for: 25 CHOOSE A TARGET
submit: demo
wait-for: 120 RUN FOCUS
keys: b
wait-for: 30 findings / 1 crit
wait: 2
# Force the workbench view first — leaving Run Focus with `b` can restore the
# Setup origin, which parks the prompt.
submit: workbench
wait: 2
submit: replay verify-escalated-run
wait-live-snap: 15 tie-break | replay-stages
expect: gate · plausibility (openai:gpt-cheap) · rejection only
expect: panel · 2 pass(es) (openai:gpt-verify)
expect: escalation · tie-break (openai:gpt-strong)
ask: Do the three stages appear in gate -> panel -> escalation ORDER with three DIFFERENT model names, each stage explaining WHY it ran (the trust rule), not just that a model was called?
keys: Escape
wait: 2
submit: replay verify-refused-run
wait-live-snap: 15 refused | replay-refused
expect: refused
expect-not: escalation · tie-break (
ask: Refusal replay — the refused row is toned Danger/Warn (check the .ansi SGR), and a refused escalation never appears as a completed `escalation · tie-break (` stage?
